* circuit-forge generic device library
*
* Ships with the tool so every seed pattern simulates out of the box with no
* downloads.  These are *generic stand-ins*, adequate for topology
* verification and tolerance studies, not for datasheet-accurate margining.
* For production numbers, drop the vendor .lib into models/ (it takes
* precedence over this file) and reference the vendor model name.
*
* Units in comments are SI base units unless stated.

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Diodes
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N4148 small-signal switching diode.
.model 1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 CJO=4p M=0.4 TT=20n BV=75 IBV=5u)

* Sharp clamp diode used by the op-amp macromodel output limiter.
* Not a real part: N is deliberately small so the clamp is stiff.
.model DCLAMP D(IS=1e-15 N=0.05 RS=0.1 CJO=0)

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Bipolar transistors
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 2N3904 general-purpose NPN (Gummel-Poon).
.model 2N3904 NPN(IS=6.734f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259
+ ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=0.7371 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1
+ CJC=3.638p MJC=0.3085 VJC=0.75 FC=0.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=0.2593 VJE=0.75
+ TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=0.4 VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* MOSFETs
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 2N7002 small-signal N-channel MOSFET, as a level-1 MOS.
* Level 1 is used instead of VDMOS for portability across ngspice builds.
* Vto = 2.0 V, Kp = 0.15 A/V^2 at W/L = 1, so gm = sqrt(2*Kp*Id).
* Instantiate with W=100u L=100u (the SPICE defaults) for a W/L of 1.
.model 2N7002 NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=2.0 KP=0.15 LAMBDA=0.01 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6
+ RD=1.5 RS=0.2 IS=1e-14 CBD=8p CBS=8p CGSO=1n CGDO=0.2n CGBO=0)

* Generic small N-channel MOSFET with a lower threshold, for 3.3 V rails.
.model NMOS_LV NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=1.0 KP=0.20 LAMBDA=0.01 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6
+ RD=1.0 RS=0.2 IS=1e-14 CBD=6p CBS=6p CGSO=1n CGDO=0.2n CGBO=0)

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Op-amp macromodel
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* OPAMP_GENERIC: single dominant pole, finite open-loop gain and output
* impedance, output clamped to within ~1.2 V of each rail.
*
*   nodes:  inp inn vcc vee out
*   Aol   = 1e5      (100 dB)
*   fp    = 10 Hz    -> GBW = 1 MHz
*   Rout  = 50 ohm
*   Rin   = 1 Mohm differential, 1 Gohm each input to ground (keeps the
*           matrix non-singular when an input would otherwise float)
*
* Patterns that care about GBW must check it against fc; see the
* GOTCHA-SK-02 gbw_margin check.
.subckt OPAMP_GENERIC inp inn vcc vee out
Rin    inp inn 1e6
Rcmp   inp 0   1e9
Rcmn   inn 0   1e9
* Transconductance stage: gm * Rgain = 1e5 open-loop gain.
Gm     0   n1  inp inn 1e-3
Rgain  n1  0   1e8
Cpole  n1  0   159.1549p
* Output clamp to (vcc - 1.2) and (vee + 1.2).
Ehi    nhi 0   vcc 0 1.0
Vhi    nhi nhic DC 1.2
Elo    nlo 0   vee 0 1.0
Vlo    nloc nlo DC 1.2
Dhi    n1  nhic DCLAMP
Dlo    nloc n1  DCLAMP
* Unity-gain output buffer with finite output impedance.
Ebuf   nout 0  n1 0 1.0
Rout   nout out 50
.ends OPAMP_GENERIC

* OPAMP_FAST: same topology, 10 MHz GBW.  Use when GOTCHA-SK-02 fires.
.subckt OPAMP_FAST inp inn vcc vee out
Rin    inp inn 1e6
Rcmp   inp 0   1e9
Rcmn   inn 0   1e9
Gm     0   n1  inp inn 1e-3
Rgain  n1  0   1e8
Cpole  n1  0   15.91549p
Ehi    nhi 0   vcc 0 1.0
Vhi    nhi nhic DC 1.2
Elo    nlo 0   vee 0 1.0
Vlo    nloc nlo DC 1.2
Dhi    n1  nhic DCLAMP
Dlo    nloc n1  DCLAMP
Ebuf   nout 0  n1 0 1.0
Rout   nout out 50
.ends OPAMP_FAST
